    "name": "Pro/Con Analysis",
    "description": "Weigh a decision — advantages, disadvantages, evaluation criteria, and costs. Ideal for platform, vendor, tool, or architecture choices. Starts as a structure; AI fills it with decision-relevant specifics.",
    "isTemplate": true,
    "templateApproved": true,
    "isFeatured": false,
    "isCommunity": true,
    "templatePrompt": "Populate the ENTIRE board in your first response. Keep the four section categories (Advantages, Disadvantages, Evaluation Criteria, Costs) exactly as they are. For the specific decision named, write 4-7 sticky notes for EACH of the four categories and return them all via the respond function immediately — roughly 20 notes total. Notes must be grounded in the named options (e.g. PostgreSQL vs MySQL): concrete tradeoffs that could change a decision ('query latency ceiling under connection pooling' yes, 'performance matters' no). Evaluation Criteria must be questions or thresholds the user can test (latency ceiling, licensing caps, migration path, lock-in risk). Costs include licensing, migration effort, training burden and lock-in with realistic magnitudes. Include exactly one short title note stating the decision being analyzed — attach it to the main topic by setting its parentCategoryIds to [\"main\"], not to any category — plus the per-category notes. Place notes only inside the template's existing categories and set parentCategoryIds to the matching category name so they attach correctly. Do not build visualizations, do not describe a plan, do not ask which category to start with — create all notes now.",
